@startuml SABER System Overview

!theme plain
title Security Agent Benchmarking System - System Overview

skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor lightblue
    BorderColor black
    ArrowColor black
    FontSize 12
}

skinparam package {
    BackgroundColor lightyellow
    BorderColor black
    FontSize 14
}

skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor lightgreen
    FontSize 10
}

package "SABER Server Side" {

    class SessionManager {
        +domain_name: str
        +active_sessions: Dict[str, ClientSession]
        +task_manager: TaskManager
        +execution_manager: ExecutionManager
        +policy_manager: PolicyManager
        +evaluation_manager: EvaluationManager
        +api: SessionAPI
        --
        +start_server(): void
        +shutdown(): void
        +create_session(): ClientSession
        +terminate_session(): void
        +start_episode(): Episode
        +step(): SessionStepResponse
        +get_current_task(): Dict[str, Any]
        +get_policy(): PolicyDocument
    }

    class TaskManager {
        +domain: str
        +tasks: Dict[str, Task]
        +config_loader: TaskConfigLoader
        +episode_manager: EpisodeManager
        --
        +get_task(): Task
        +get_subtask(): SubTask
        +start_episode(): Episode
        +step(session_id, action, command_result?): Step
        +reset(): Episode
        +end_episode(): Episode
        +list_tasks(): List[Dict]
    }

    class ExecutionManager {
        --
        +step(): CommandResult
        +validate_command(): ValidationResult
        +list_commands(): List[Dict[str, Any]]
        +get_security_info(): Dict[str, Any]
        +get_execution_stats(): Dict[str, Any]
        +to_mcp_tools(): List[Dict[str, Any]]
        +_determine_executor_type(): str
    }

    class PolicyManager {
        +domain_policy: PolicyDocument
        --
        +get_policy(): PolicyDocument
        +validate_action(): bool
    }

    class EvaluationManager {
        +trajectory_store: TrajectoryStore
        +action_tracker: ActionTracker
        --
        +log_action(): void
        +get_trajectory(): List[ActionRecord]
    }
}

package "SABER Client Side" {

    class TestHarness {
        +config: TestHarnessConfig
        +server_client: ServerClient
        +agent: Any
        +session_id: str?
        --
        +initialize(agent: Any): void
        +run_test(): Dict[str, Any]
        +shutdown(): void
    }

    class ServerClient {
        +server_url: str
        +session_id: str?
        --
        +create_session(): str
        +start_episode(): EpisodeInfo
        +execute_step(): StepResponse
        +get_current_task(): TaskInfo
        +get_policy(): PolicyInfo
        +close_session(): void
    }

    class AgentWrapper {
        +agent: Any
        +process_method: Callable
        +is_async: bool
        --
        +process_prompt(): str
        +reset(): void
    }

    class AgentLoader {
        --
        +load_from_path(): AgentWrapper
        +load_from_module(): AgentWrapper
    }

    class CLI {
        --
        +main(): void
    }
}

' Server Internal Relationships
SessionManager *-- TaskManager
SessionManager *-- ExecutionManager
SessionManager *-- PolicyManager
SessionManager *-- EvaluationManager

' Client Internal Relationships
TestHarness *-- ServerClient
TestHarness *-- AgentWrapper
AgentLoader ..> AgentWrapper : creates
CLI ..> TestHarness : orchestrates

' Client-Server Communication
ServerClient ..> SessionManager : "HTTP REST API"
TestHarness ..> SessionManager : "via ServerClient"

note top of SessionManager
**SABER Domain Server & Session Manager**
- Hosts one security domain (horizontally scalable)
- Manages multiple concurrent client sessions
- Single unified entry point for all client interactions
- Integrates ExecutionManager for Docker sandbox command execution
- Coordinates task execution and command processing
- Provides REST API for command execution and task management
- Built for horizontal scaling with load balancing
end note

note top of ExecutionManager
**Command Execution Manager**
- Factory-based executor management supporting CLI and Python execution
- Manages Docker-based command execution with security validation
- Provides command listing and security information
- Handles execution statistics and performance monitoring
- Scalable architecture supporting multiple executor types
- See command_execution_architecture.puml for detailed design
end note

note left of TestHarness
**SABER Test Harness & Client**
- Orchestrates agent testing workflow
- Manages server communication via ServerClient
- Wraps customer agents via AgentWrapper
- Handles session lifecycle and test execution
- Provides clean separation between agent logic and communication
- CLI provides command-line interface for test execution
end note

note top of AgentWrapper
**Agent Under Test Interface**
- Wraps customer-provided AI agent implementations
- Configurable LLM provider (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.)
- Domain-specific reasoning and planning capabilities
- Receives task context, policy, and guidelines
- Generates commands based on security analysis
- Processes results and adapts strategy
- Isolated from server communication details
end note

@enduml
